33
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Miss Misato, it's morning already

34
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:36,000
I just got back from night duty a little while ago

35
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
I don't have to go to work until this evening

36
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,000
so please let me sleep

37
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Okay, I'll go

38
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Hey, is this okay Thursday?

39
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
It's burnable trash day

40
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Take it to the garbage please

41
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Okay

42
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
So how's school?

43
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Oh, it's okay

44
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Okay, see you

45
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
I'll see you later

46
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Yes, hello?

47
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Oh, it's you, Itsuko

48
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,000
How's it going? Are you getting along with him?

49
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Him? Oh, Shinji

50
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Well, it's been two weeks since he started school

51
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
And he doesn't seem to have changed

52
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:32,000
No one ever calls him

53
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Calls him where?

54
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Well, since I figured he'd be needing one

55
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
I gave him a cellular phone

56
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,000
I don't think he's ever used it though

57
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Or received any calls

58
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
I'm not sure

59
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
But I don't think he has any friends

60
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Well, I would guess that Shinji isn't exactly the sort of person who makes friends easily

61
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Mm-hmm

62
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Do you know the fable, The Hedgehog's Dilemma?

63
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Hedgehog?

64
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,000
You mean those animals with the spiny hair?

65
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Even though a hedgehog may want to become close with another hedgehog

66
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
The closer they get, the more they injure each other with their spines

67
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Hmm

68
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
It's the same with some humans

69
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:13,000
The reason he seems so withdrawn is because he's afraid of being hurt

70
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Well, he's just going to have to learn

71
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Someday

72
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
That part of growing up means

73
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Finding a way to interact with others

74
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
While distancing pain

75
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:41,000
What's up, class rep?

76
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Did you deliver the printout I gave you yesterday?

77
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,000
What?

78
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Um, well, um, um

79
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Well, um, there wasn't anybody home over at Toji's place

80
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Mr. Ida, aren't you Suzuhara's friend?

81
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:55,000
Aren't you even just a little bit worried about him?

82
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,000
You don't suppose he was injured, do you?

83
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
What? You mean in that robot incident?

84
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,000
The television reports all said that nobody was injured

85
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,000
No way!

86
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,000
You saw where the explosion on Mount Takanosu was, didn't you?

87
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,000
There were fighters scrambled from a room in Komatsu

88
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,000
And there were troops from Isawa and Kyushu

89
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
I'll bet at least 10 or 20 people were injured

90
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
And there had to be a few fatalities, too

91
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Toji!

92
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Susuhara!

93
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Where is everyone?

94
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Has our entire class disappeared or what?

95
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:27,000
They've all either evacuated or they've transferred to other schools

96
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,000
No one wants to stay here after that last battle inside the city

97
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Yeah, you're probably the only one who's actually enjoying the chance to see a real war

98
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,000
That's true!

99
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,000
And speaking of which, where have you been, Toji?

100
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Why were you absent so long?

101
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Did you get involved in the war?

102
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
No, but my little sister did

103
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Ah!

104
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:50,000
She was crushed under a pile of debris

105
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:55,000
She survived, but she's been in the hospital ever since

106
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Both my dad and granddad are working at the lab

107
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
And there's no way they can leave their posts

108
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:04,000
So, if I'm not with her, she's all alone

109
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:07,000
That robot's pilot was really dumb!

110
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,000
It made me so angry!

111
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
How could he wreck our own city?

112
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
What did that stupid idiot think he was doing?

113
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:17,000
Speaking of the pilot, have you heard the rumor about the transfer student?

114
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
What transfer student?

115
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Him, over there!

116
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,000
He transferred in while you were absent

117
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Right after the giant robot incident

118
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Don't you think that's a little bit of an odd coincidence?

119
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,000
Shut up! He's coming!

120
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,000
All rise!

121
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:39,000
And so, humankind was about to face its greatest trial

122
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,000
In the last year of the 20th century

123
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
The massive meteor from outer space

124
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,000
Slammed into the continent of Antarctica

125
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:49,000
The continent's ice cap was melted almost instantaneously

126
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:53,000
The water level of the oceans increased dramatically

127
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,000
The Earth was thrown off its axis

128
00:07:55,000 --> 00:08:00,000
And new devastatingly abnormal weather patterns were spawned

129
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:04,000
The lives of all living things on the planet were threatened

130
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Several thousand species of flora and fauna

131
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
And half of the world's human population

132
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
Were lost in the immediate aftermath of the disaster

133
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:17,000
That was the so-called second impact

134
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:22,000
The survivors still had to live through the hell of worldwide economic collapse

135
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,000
Ethnic conflicts and civil wars

136
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:31,000
However, it has been 15 years since then

137
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,000
And in only 15 years we have restored ourselves

138
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:38,000
This is certainly proof of the human race's resilience

139
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:40,000
But even more so

140
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:43,000
It is the fruit of the blood, sweat and tears

141
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:46,000
Your father and mothers have dedicated to this cause

142
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
I lived and never found

143
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:51,000
Hey, sit down, you guys! We're still in class, you know!

144
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Sit down now!

145
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,000
You're always so...

146
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Now cut that out!

147
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Do you think I can get anywhere?

148
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
Well, you know...

149
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Hey, how did you get chosen?

150
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Did you have to take a test?

151
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Weren't you really scared?

152
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,000
What's a cockpit look like?

153
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:09,000
I'm not supposed to talk about classified stuff like that

154
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:13,000
Hey, what's the name of that robot?

155
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:18,000
I don't know much, but everyone calls it Ava or Unit 1

156
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Ava?

157
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
What's its ultimate attack mode?

158
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,000
Some kind of vibrating knife

159
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
An ultrasonic wave

160
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
That's amazing! We are so proud of you!

161
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:32,000
And thus...

162
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Oh...

163
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
That's all for the day

164
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Ikari, where do you live?

165
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
In the outer part of the city?

166
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Everybody stand up!

167
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Belle!

168
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
Hey, you guys, can't you at least show some manners?

169
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,000
Sorry, newcomer, but I had to clobber you

170
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,000
I had to pop you one to work off my own anger

171
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
He's mean, huh?

172
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:04,000
His little sister was injured the last time you and your robot fought a battle

173
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Well, that's his excuse anyway

174
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:09,000
I didn't have a choice

175
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
They made me pilot the stupid thing

176
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Uh uh

177
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Uh...

178
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Ghhhhh

179
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,000
Huh?

180
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:45,000
There's an emergency. I'll report in first.

181
00:10:54,000 --> 00:11:00,000
A special state of emergency has been declared for the Kanto and Chuga regions surrounding the Tokai district.

182
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:05,000
All residents must evacuate to their designated shelters immediately.

183
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Our cameras have sighted the target. It's penetrated our territorial waters.

184
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Assume battle stations. Level one.

185
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Roger. Prepare for anti-aircraft interception.

186
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Tokyo-3, transforming to battle formation.

187
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,000
Initiate accommodation of the central block.

188
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Jumping out, you Oyster on theannie.

189
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Weót.

190
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,000
nezATOR CT.

191
00:11:43,000 --> 00:12:11,240
Accommodation of the central block in the first through seven districts has been completed.

192
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:14,440
Notification of the government and other related ministries completed.

193
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:18,240
Present effective rate of anti-aircraft interception, 48 percent.

194
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:21,240
Status of civilians and non-combatants?

195
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:24,240
We've received reports that civilian evacuation has been completed.

196
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:29,240
Attention elementary school and junior high school students.

197
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:32,240
Please form groups with your individual classes.

198
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:35,240
Not again! Just text messages again?

199
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:40,240
It's no censorship. The government won't let them show any of the battle to us civilians.

200
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:47,240
Even though it's an incredible historic event.

201
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:50,240
The fourth angel would show up while Commander Ikari is away.

202
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:52,240
It's a lot sooner than we expected.

203
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:54,240
The last time they gave us 15 years.

204
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:56,240
This time around the break's only been three weeks.

205
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:59,240
They never care about our situation, do they?

206
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:01,240
They're the kind we women hate the most.

207
00:13:08,240 --> 00:13:10,240
It's a waste of the taxpayers' money.

208
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:13,240
The committee is demanding that we dispatch an Evangelion again.

209
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:18,240
They're more obnoxious than the aliens. I'd have mobilized even if they hadn't asked.

210
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:22,240
Entry procedure initiated.

211
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:27,240
LCL oxygenated. Releasing airlock.

212
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:44,240
Hey, I need to talk to you privately for a second.

213
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:45,240
I want four.

214
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,240
Come on, please.

215
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:48,240
Oh, all right.

216
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:50,240
Hey, class rep!

217
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:51,240
Now what?

218
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:54,240
We've both gotta go to the bathroom.

219
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:57,240
You were supposed to do that before you came here.

220
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:59,240
So what's this all about?

221
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:01,240
I've gotta see it at least once in my life.

222
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:03,240
You mean the battle up there?

223
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:06,240
Nobody knows when the enemy will come the next time.

224
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:08,240
Kensuke, are you serious?

225
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:12,240
If we let this opportunity escape us, we may lose it forever.

226
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:15,240
Please, help me unlock the gate.

227
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:17,240
But you can get killed if you go out there.

228
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:21,240
If we stay here in the shelter, who's to say that the risk isn't the same?

229
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:24,240
If I might be killed anyway, I'd rather see it first.

230
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:27,240
You idiot. What do you think Nerve's for?

231
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:30,240
And what is Nerve's most important weapon?

232
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,240
It's the robot that new kid pilots.

233
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:35,240
He protected us the other day, but you hit him pretty hard.

234
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:37,240
Twice.

235
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:41,240
If he refuses to fight, we're all going to die.

236
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:44,240
Doesn't that make it your obligation to watch him fight?

237
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:47,240
Okay, you're not leaving me any options.

238
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:51,240
You'll do just about anything to get what you want, won't you?

239
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:56,240
Shinji, are you ready?

240
00:14:56,240 --> 00:15:00,240
First, neutralize the enemy's AT field, then fire a volley.

241
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:02,240
Do it just like we practiced.

242
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:04,240
Can you handle that?

243
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,240
Launch, Ava!

244
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,240
Launch, Ava!

245
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:27,240
Cool! All my efforts really paid off!

246
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:30,240
I've been waiting for this moment all my life!

247
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:39,240
Whoa!

248
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,240
There it is!

249
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:45,240
The AT field has been unfolded.

250
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:47,240
Do it just like we planned, okay, Shinji?

251
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:48,240
Okay!

252
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,240
Okay!

253
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,240
Idiot!

254
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:57,240
You hit the enemy with your own smoke!

255
00:15:57,240 --> 00:16:09,240
I don't believe it!

256
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:10,240
He's losing already!

257
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:11,240
It's not a problem.

258
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,240
I'm sending you a spare rifle!

259
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:13,240
Take it!

260
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:14,240
Shiji!

261
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:15,240
Shiji!

262
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:16,240
Shiji!

